{"name":"Narvik","hex":"#e9e6dc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Narvik","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A town and municipality in Ofoten district, Nordland, Norway."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Narvik"}],"entries":[{"title":"Narvik (town)","blocks":[{"text":"(Norwegian) or Áhkánjárga (Northern Sami) is a town and the administrative centre of Narvik Municipality in Nordland county, Norway. The town is located along the Ofotfjorden in the Ofoten region. The town lies on a peninsula located between the Rombaken fjord and the Beisfjorden. The European route E06 highway runs through the Beisfjord Bridge and Hålogaland Bridge crossing the two small fjords surrounding the town."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Fjellheis_Narvik_57.JPG/330px-Fjellheis_Narvik_57.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narvik_(town)","wikidata":"Q59101"},{"title":"Narvik (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Narvik is a Norwegian historical film depicting the Battles of Narvik from 9 April to 8 June 1940. Directed by Erik Skjoldbjærg and made by Nordisk Film, it stars Kristine Hartgen, Carl Martin Eggesbø, Cristoph Gelfert Mathiesen and Henrik Mestad. The film premiered in Norway in December 2022 and was released worldwide on Netflix in January 2023."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/de/Narvik_%28film%29_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narvik_(film)","wikidata":"Q97200579"},{"title":"Narvik Municipality","blocks":[{"text":"Narvik is the third-largest municipality in Nordland county, Norway, by population. The administrative centre of the municipality is the town of Narvik. Some of the notable villages in the municipality include Ankenesstrand, Ballangen, Beisfjord, Bjerkvik, Bjørnfjell, Elvegården, Kjøpsvik, Skjomen, Håkvik, Hergot, Straumsnes, and Vidrek. The Elvegårdsmoen army camp is located near Bjerkvik."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Narvik_from_above.JPG/330px-Narvik_from_above.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narvik_Municipality","wikidata":"Q1215658"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Narvik1.jpg/500px-Narvik1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Narvik1.jpg/1280px-Narvik1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Narvik1.jpg/500px-Narvik1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Near Narvik city centre; Ankenes is seen across the bay","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANarvik1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Narvik%2C_Norway_-_panoramio_%282%29.jpg/500px-Narvik%2C_Norway_-_panoramio_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Narvik%2C_Norway_-_panoramio_%282%29.jpg/1280px-Narvik%2C_Norway_-_panoramio_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Narvik%2C_Norway_-_panoramio_%282%29.jpg/500px-Narvik%2C_Norway_-_panoramio_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Narvik guest harbor","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANarvik%2C_Norway_-_panoramio_(2).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Lapland1940.png/330px-Lapland1940.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikip